First, we recall the difference formula for tangent:

$$
\tan(u-v) = \dfrac{\tan{u}-\tan{v}}{1+\tan{u}\tan{v}}
$$

Applying the difference formula for tangent with $u=x$ and

$$
v=\dfrac{\pi}{4}
$$

we obtain

$$
\begin{aligned}
\tan (x - \frac{π}{4}) &= (\tan x - \tan \left(\frac{π}{4}\right))/(1 + \tan x\tan \left(\frac{π}{4}\right)) \\
&= \frac{\tan x - 1}{1 + \tan x \cdot 1} \\
&= \frac{\tan x - 1}{\tan x + 1}
\end{aligned}
$$

